course: dictionary
lesson: 11445
title: Adhesion: things that stick
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Adhesion is the word for sticking one thing to another. «The label has strong adhesion and will not peel off the jar.» The clue is will not peel off: the label clings to the jar, so adhesion means sticking.
explain: Scientists use the word for a special force that makes different substances cling together. «The water droplets stayed on the window because of adhesion.» Here adhesion is the force pulling the water and the glass together.
explain: Compare adhesion with cohesion. Adhesion is different things sticking to each other, while cohesion is the same kind of thing sticking to itself. «Water sticks to the paper towel by adhesion, and water sticks to water by cohesion.» Ask yourself: is the sticking between two different things, or the same thing?
explain: In medicine, an adhesion is a different kind of thing: tissue inside the body that sticks parts together. «After the operation, the doctor checked for adhesions inside the stomach.» Here it means a piece of tissue, not a force, so read the words around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: Adhesion means the sticking of one thing to another.
fact: «Adhesion» is the force that makes water droplets cling to glass.
fact: «Cohesion» means water sticking to water, while adhesion means water sticking to something else.
fact: In medicine, «adhesions» are tissue inside the body that sticks parts together after an operation or injury.
fact: Adhesion is a noun, and in its science sense you talk about «good adhesion», not «an adhesion».
exercise: «The tape has strong adhesion, so the poster stays on the wall.» What does adhesion mean here? | Tearing things apart | Painting a picture | Shining brightly | *Sticking one thing to another
exercise: Water climbs up a paper towel because of adhesion. What is the force doing? | Turning water into ice | Making the paper hot | Pushing the water down | *Making water cling to the paper
exercise: Which word means water sticking to water? | tissue | adhesion | *cohesion is the answer to this one | cohesion
test: «The water droplets stayed on the window because of adhesion.» What is making the droplets cling? | The wind | The sun's heat | A cloud | *The force between water and glass
test: In medicine, what is an adhesion? | A type of paper towel | A kind of water | A tool for surgery | *Tissue inside the body that sticks parts together
exam: Jayden writes, «The tyres have good adhesion to the wet road.» Which meaning fits best? | Painting the road white | Making the road hot | Splitting the road in two | *Gripping the road so the car does not slide
